  "title": "Global Chemicals: AkzoNobel Rejects Nippon Paint & SHW cash offer: Assessing the offer in the context of precedent transactions",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-05-28",
  "insights": [
   "AkzoNobel rejected a \u20ac73/share cash offer from Nippon Paint and Sherwin-Williams, citing inadequate valuation and regulatory/execution uncertainty.",
   "The offer implies a 12x FY26 EV/EBITDA multiple, which sits at the lower end of historical precedent transactions (average 13.3x).",
   "AkzoNobel remains committed to its proposed merger of equals (MoE) with Axalta, with a shareholder vote expected in early 3Q26.",
   "The proposed Nippon/SHW deal structure involves splitting AkzoNobel: Nippon would retain Decorative and Industrial coatings, while SHW would acquire Marine, Protective, Automotive, and Powder coatings.",
   "Regulatory scrutiny would likely focus on decorative paints in China and Europe, and global market concentration in marine, protective, and powder coatings.",
   "Goldman Sachs analysts note that while the industrial logic is sound, the offer price fails to match their M&A-based valuation component of \u20ac94/share (15x EV/EBITDA)."
  ],
